miadi-server — the Miadi web app as a per-user service

  sudo apt install miadi-server

The package holds a launcher and a per-user systemd unit. The checkout, its
dependencies and its build stay with the checkout, and the package starts
nothing.

Set up a host, as the user who will run the service:

  git clone https://github.com/jgwill/Miadi.git <checkout>
  sudo miadi-config set MIADI_PROJECT_DIR <checkout>
  cd <checkout> && pnpm install
  pnpm --filter "miadi-project^..." --filter "@miadi/voice-client..." run build     # install does not build these
  pnpm build
  miadi-server check
  systemctl --user enable --now miadi-server
  sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"     # so it starts at boot, with nobody logged in

Building needs pnpm and npm on PATH, and the checkout's .env. miadi-node, which runs the service, carries neither.

Three host settings, in /etc/miadi/miadi.env through `sudo miadi-config set`:

  MIADI_PROJECT_DIR   the checkout, else MIADI_SRC
  MIADI_MODE_FILE     a file holding dev or prod (default /etc/miadi/mode);
                      no file means prod
  MIADI_PORT          the port (default 3335)

The app's own settings stay in the checkout's .env. The launcher passes the
app nothing else from miadi.env, so a host value such as MIADI_URL_BASE has
to be set in .env as well to reach the app.

Rebuild an installed service with scripts/ops/miadi-refresh.sh in the
checkout. It builds beside the running server and swaps the build in.

The app needs two services it can reach: the Redis in KV_REST_API_URL and
the medicine wheel in MIADI_CHRONICLE_MW_URL. Without the wheel, person
tokens answer 502.

Person and seat tokens are checked against credentials.jsonl in
MIADI_IDENTITY_DIR (default /srv/miadi/identity), a file local to each host.
A new host needs that file from the host that issued the tokens, or new
tokens from its own /me page.

An exit status of 2 from miadi-server is a setup problem. The unit does not
restart on it, and `miadi-server check` names it.

  journalctl --user -u miadi-server

Source: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit, packages/miadi/deb
